<title>USA: CME Sept S&amp;P 500s fall initial 15-pt daily limit.</title>
<headline>CME Sept S&amp;P 500s fall initial 15-pt daily limit.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Mercantile Exchange's (CME) September Standard &amp; Poor's 500 futures fell the initial 15-point daily limit.</p>
<p>According to exchange rules, a two-minute trading halt will be imposed if September remains locked at the limit at the end of 15 minutes.</p>
<p>The next downside limit is 30 points.</p>
<p>((Chicago Derivatives desk 312-408-8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
